// =====================================================================================
// 2x UI - Minimal panels  (optional sub-choice of the 2x UI component; install AFTER it)
// =====================================================================================
// The 2x UI ships DECORATED panel backgrounds: GCOMM118 / GCOMM128 (command bar), GMWDMMB0 /
// GMWDSLB0 (world map), GUCONTB0 (container), GUDEATH0 (death), GUWBTP30 (worldmap travel) -- each
// 2048px wide = the 1600px content centred + a decorative stone frame extending ~224px each side
// into the letterbox void.
//
// This sub-choice swaps in MINIMAL versions (mos/mos_2x_minimal). They are the SAME content centred in the
// SAME 2048 canvas, but the void margins are GREEN-KEYED (palette index 0) = TRANSPARENT, so the
// world / menu scene shows through instead of the stone decoration. WHY keep 2048 + centre + pad
// transparent (instead of just the narrower 1600 minimal MOS): the engine renders a panel background at
// the panel's TOP-LEFT origin (CUIPanel::Render), and these panels are laid out for the 2048 decorated
// width -- a bare 1600 MOS would render left-aligned, mis-aligning the controls + leaving the right
// margin uncovered. Padding the content to a centred 2048 keeps the controls aligned; the transparent
// margins remove the decoration cleanly.
//
// Resref-for-resref overwrite of the decorated backgrounds, so the panels (which reference the
// decorated resrefs) pick the minimal art with no layout change. To wire into the installer, add a tp2
// BEGIN block alongside the 2x UI component, e.g. a SUBCOMPONENT pairing "Decorated" (the 2x UI default)
// with "Minimal" (this), REQUIRE_COMPONENT the 2x UI.
// =====================================================================================

PRINT ~[2x UI] Minimal panels: replacing the decorative void frame with transparent margins.~
COPY ~%mod_folder%/mos/mos_2x_minimal~ ~override~
